**Read:** [Multizone airflow and contaminants — Dols and Polidoro, CONTAM 3.4](../sources/CONTAM-Multizone-Airflow-and-Contaminants-NIST.lingua#r_5HECDC480RSYAJ3SQ2QNFHCN46), complete chapter 8.2, especially printed page 251.

For constant-density mixed zones, define each directed Qij≥0 as flow from i to j. Then Vi dCi/dt=Gi+Σj PjiQjiCj−(Σj Qij+kiVi)Ci, where Pji is penetration along that incoming path and ki is an internal first-order removal rate. An outdoor node can have a prescribed concentration. A self-loop represents recirculation and reduces to its net filtered removal.

Choose upstream concentration after resolving the flow direction. Simultaneous counterflows need separate directed terms even when their net airflow is zero. At steady state these equations form a coupled linear system once the flows and coefficients are fixed. Non-trace mixtures or changing density require an air-mass and species-mass formulation rather than this simplified volume model.

**Work:** Use the preceding two-room network with clean mechanical supply and outdoor air, no filtration/deposition, and sources G1=1 and G2=0.1 particles/s. Find C1=20 and C2≈23.2632 particles/m³, then verify that all external and mechanical exhaust together removes 1.1 particles/s. Recompute after the pressure reversal. Add a transient inventory and show internal transfers cancel when the room balances are summed.

